Sval: the content classifier parses trusted lists with adblock-rust's trusted bit

uBlock Origin marks some scriptlets as needing trust, and adblock-rust gives
them permission bit 0: a `##+js()` rule runs one only when the list it came
from was parsed with that bit in ParseOptions.permissions. The engine crate
parsed every list with default ParseOptions, so none ran. The service reads
privacy.trackingprotection.content.trusted_list_ids, the lists Sval trusts,
and hands the engine crate each rule's permission bits with its rules; the
crate parses each run of rules with their bits into one FilterSet. A list
that gains or loses trust rebuilds the engines that use it, through
ProcessListChanges.

The rules reach adblock-rust inside ContentClassifierService and the engine
crate's FFI, so no chrome API can set a list's parse options.

